# Keyboard Diagram Fixes

## Issue
The Control key was not being highlighted in the keyboard diagram when shortcuts containing Control were active.

## Root Cause
- The keyboard layout had the Control key labeled as "Ctrl" (abbreviated)
- The shortcuts system stored the key name as "Control" (full name)
- When checking if a key should be highlighted, the comparison was:
  - "CTRL" (from keyboard layout) vs "CONTROL" (from shortcuts)
  - These didn't match, so highlighting failed

## Solution
### File: `static/assets/js/settings-page.js`

1. **Line 381**: Changed keyboard layout bottom row from:
   ```javascript
   { keys: ["Ctrl", "Alt", "Space", "Alt", "Ctrl"], sizes: [1.25, 1.25, 6, 1.25, 1.25] }
   ```
   To:
   ```javascript
   { keys: ["Control", "Alt", "Space", "Alt", "Control"], sizes: [1.25, 1.25, 6, 1.25, 1.25] }
   ```
   This ensures the internal key name matches the shortcuts storage.

2. **Line 418**: Updated key display to show "Ctrl" abbreviation while maintaining "Control" internally:
   ```javascript
   const displayKey = key === "Control" ? "Ctrl" : (key !== "Space" ? key : "");
   keyEl.textContent = displayKey;
   ```

## Result
- Control key now properly highlights when Control+K (Command Box) shortcut is active
- UI shows "Ctrl" for readability
- Internal key matching works correctly

---

# Personalization Tab Feature

## Changes Made

### 1. HTML - Settings Panel (`static/settings.html`)
- Added new "Personalization" tab button with custom SVG icon in the settings sidebar
- Added new personalization panel with three main sections:
  - **Appearance**: Background image upload and color picker
  - **Visibility**: Toggle switches for:
    - Infrared logo display
    - Navigation bar display
    - Tips display

### 2. CSS Styles (`static/assets/css/settings.css`)
- `.toggle-switch`: Styled toggle switch with smooth transitions
  - Width: 52px, Height: 28px
  - Active state: Cyan highlight (rgba(100, 200, 255, ...))
  - Slider animation on checked state
- `.toggle-slider`: Visual toggle slider with ::after pseudo-element
- `.personalization-btn`: Button for uploading background images
  - Cyan highlight theme matching other UI elements
- `#bg-color-input`: Styled color picker (50x40px)

### 3. JavaScript - Settings Logic (`static/assets/js/settings-page.js`)
- `PERSONALIZATION_KEY`: localStorage key for storing settings
- `getPersonalizationSettings()`: Retrieves settings from localStorage with defaults
- `savePersonalizationSettings()`: Saves settings and applies them immediately
- `applyPersonalizationSettings()`: Applies settings to current window and iframes
- `initPersonalization()`: Initializes UI and event listeners:
  - Toggle switches: Show/hide logo, navbar, tips
  - Color picker: Change background color
  - File upload: Upload custom background image

### 4. Home Page Integration (`static/index.html`)
- `loadPersonalizationSettings()`: Loads and applies saved settings on page load
- Applies background image/color to `.wallpaper` element
- Toggles visibility of:
  - `.title` (Infrared logo)
  - `.navbar` (navigation bar)
  - `#dynamic-subtitle` (tips)

## Data Storage
- **Key**: `infraredPersonalization`
- **Format**: JSON object with properties:
  ```json
  {
    "backgroundImage": "data:image/...[base64]" or null,
    "backgroundColor": "#1a1a1a",
    "showLogo": true,
    "showNavbar": true,
    "showTips": true
  }
  ```

## Feature Behavior
- Settings persist across page refreshes using localStorage
- Background images are stored as base64 data URLs
- Changes apply immediately to the home page
- All settings default to showing/enabled on first load
- UI uses cyan highlight color (rgba(100, 200, 255, ...)) matching Infrared theme

---

# Personalization UI & Hidden Navigation Updates

## Spacing & Layout Fixes

### 1. Toggle Switch Styling (`static/assets/css/settings.css`)
- Increased toggle switch size: 52px → 56px width, 28px → 32px height
- Added padding to toggle-switch: 12px vertical
- Improved toggle slider dimensions: 22px → 24px diameter circle
- Better slider position on checked: left 26px → 27px
- Enhanced visual spacing for better readability

### 2. Personalization Tab Icon (`static/settings.html`)
- Updated icon from clock/timer to palette icon
- Better represents personalization/customization feature
- SVG path: Palette with dot accent showing customization theme

## Hidden Navigation Bar (Top Hover)

### 3. Hidden Navigation Overlay CSS (`static/assets/css/nav.css`)
- `.hidden-nav-overlay`: Fixed overlay at top of page
  - Height: 50px
  - Only visible on hover when navbar is hidden
  - Smooth opacity transition (0.3s)
  
- `.hidden-nav-links`: Hidden quick access links
  - Position: Top-right corner
  - Links: "Tabs" and "Settings"
  - Appears on hover above the page content
  - Cyan highlight theme matching Infrared
  - Semi-transparent dark background with blur effect

### 4. Home Page HTML (`static/index.html`)
- Added hidden-nav-overlay element before main content
- Contains two quick-access links:
  - Tabs: `/d`
  - Settings: `/c`
- Only displayed when navbar is hidden (personalization setting)

### 5. Personalization JavaScript Updates (`static/assets/js/settings-page.js` & `static/index.html`)
- Updated `applyPersonalizationSettings()` to manage hidden nav overlay
- Added class toggle: `navbar-hidden` when navbar is hidden
- Hidden nav overlay appears at top when navbar is disabled
- Smooth hover reveal with backdrop blur effect

## Behavior
- When navbar is visible: Hidden nav overlay is inactive
- When navbar is hidden: Hidden nav overlay becomes active and appears on hover
- Hover zone is 50px at the top of the page
- Links quickly fade in with backdrop-filter blur effect
- Settings persist when toggling navbar visibility
   This provides consistent naming throughout the codebase while showing the abbreviated "Ctrl" in the UI.

## Result
- Control key now properly highlights when Control+K (Command Box) shortcut is active
- UI shows "Ctrl" for readability
- Internal key matching works correctly
